\image(figures/de_boor_nonuniform.svg)
// result_end
\caption(A nonuniform quadratic construction. Control index three is inactive at this parameter. Descending update order explains why local index two is listed before local index one in the first round.)
\alttext(Left: interpolation points use unequal first-round knot weights, with the final point at five thirds, eight thirds. Right: the two-piece curve approaches the fourth control after passing its interior knot; the evaluated point is highlighted.)

>> Repeated knots: a corner and a discontinuity

For the quadratic with controls \((0,0),(1,2),(2,0),(3,2),(4,0)\) and knots
\((0,0,0,1,1,2,2,2)\), the double interior knot at one allows a corner. Both
pieces meet at \(P_2=(2,0)\), but their one-sided parameter derivatives are
\(2(P_2-P_1)=(2,-4)\) and \(2(P_3-P_2)=(2,4)\).

A degree-one spline with controls \((0,0),(1,1),(2,3),(3,2)\) and knots
\((0,0,1,1,2,2)\) has full multiplicity at one. Its two straight pieces need not meet:

$$
 C(1^-)=(1,1),\qquad C(1) = C(1^+)=(2,3).
$$
\alttext(The discontinuous linear curve approaches one, one from the left and takes the right-hand value two, three at the repeated knot.)

`nextafter(1,0)` and `nextafter(1,2)` select the adjacent representable parameters.
The displayed rounding makes both look like one; their distinct span indices reveal
the side convention. The curve helper leaves the jump visibly disconnected.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/de_boor_repeated.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const dm::geometry::DeBoorSpline corner(2,{0,0,0,1,1,2,2,2},{{0,0},{1,2},{2,0},{3,2},{4,0}});
  const dm::geometry::DeBoorSpline jump(1,{0,0,1,1,2,2},{{0,0},{1,1},{2,3},{3,2}});
  auto continuous=corner.plot_curve(), discontinuous=jump.plot_curve();
  continuous.title("Double quadratic knot: a corner").y_limits(-.3,4)
    .points({2},{0},"t = 1",{220,90,35},6);
  discontinuous.title("Double linear knot: a jump").y_limits(-.3,5)
    .points({jump.evaluate(1).x},{jump.evaluate(1).y},"Right value",{220,90,35},6);
  auto layout=dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2); layout.add(continuous).add(discontinuous);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  layout.size(1100,490).fit_panels().save_svg("build/de_boor_repeated.svg");
  std::print("{}\n",jump.sample_table({std::nextafter(1.0,0.0),1,std::nextafter(1.0,2.0)}).to_md(9));
}
```
