\caption(The same multiplicity has different consequences at different degrees. Grey lines are control polygons; the blue spline pieces have no connecting segment across the jump.)
\alttext(Left: two quadratic arches meet at a sharp corner at two, zero. Right: one blue line ends at one, one, and another starts at two, three, with a gap between them. Only the grey control polygon spans that gap.)

> Checking the theory

>> Closed-form Bezier families and exact operation counts

For degree \(p\geq1\), take \(P_j=(j/p,(j/p)^2)\), with zero and one each repeated
\(p+1\) times. The weights are binomial probabilities for \(J\sim\mathrm{Binomial}(p,t)\).
Using \(E[J]=pt\) and \(E[J^2]=p^2t^2+pt(1-t)\) gives the exact curve

$$
 C_p(t)=\left(t,t^2+\frac{t(1-t)}p\right),\qquad
 \#\text{point interpolations}=\frac{p(p+1)}2.
$$
\alttext(The generated Bezier family has horizontal coordinate t and vertical coordinate t squared plus t times one minus t divided by p. Evaluation uses p times p plus one over two point blends.)

The curve is not exactly the parabola through the controls; for finite degree the
second coordinate lies above it in the interior. We check degrees one through twelve
at 101 parameters, and count actual recorded updates after the initial controls.
For every degree we also scale the knot domain to [0, 1e-15], sample three points,
and check the last sample against the exact endpoint control.
The count measures the recurrence, not validation, span-search time or wall-clock speed.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/de_boor_theory.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const auto grid=dm::seql(0,1,101);
  std::vector<double> degrees,updates,exact_counts,endpoint_errors;
  std::vector<std::string> errors;
  auto family=dm::graphics::RPlot::create(), cost=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  const std::vector<dm::RGB> colours{{37,99,235},{220,90,35},{25,145,105},{150,70,180}};
  std::size_t colour=0;
  for (int p=1;p<=12;++p) {
    std::vector<double> knots(p+1,0); knots.insert(knots.end(),p+1,1);
    std::vector<dm::geometry::Point2D> control;
    for (int j=0;j<=p;++j) {const double x=static_cast<double>(j)/p; control.push_back({x,x*x});}
    const dm::geometry::DeBoorSpline spline(p,knots,control);
    const auto samples=spline.sample_table(grid.values());
    const dm::Vector<> actual=samples.numeric_column("y").values();
    const auto error=dm::abs(actual-(grid*grid+grid*(1-grid)/p));
    degrees.push_back(p); updates.push_back(spline.trace(.375).steps.size()-(p+1));
    exact_counts.push_back(p*(p+1)/2); errors.push_back(std::format("{:.3e}",*std::max_element(error.begin(),error.end())));
    auto tiny_knots=knots; for (auto& u : tiny_knots) u*=1e-15;
    const auto tiny=dm::geometry::DeBoorSpline(p,tiny_knots,control).sample(3);
    endpoint_errors.push_back(dm::geometry::distance(tiny.back(),control.back()));
    if (p==1 || p==2 || p==4 || p==12) family.lines(grid.values(),actual.values(),std::format("p = {}",p),colours[colour++]);
  }
  family.title("A closed-form family of Bezier curves").x_label("t = C_x(t)").y_label("C_y(t)").y_limits(0,1.7);
  cost.lines(degrees,exact_counts,"p(p+1)/2",{80,80,80},3).points(degrees,updates,"Trace count",{37,99,235},4)
    .title("Quadratic work in the spline degree").x_label("Degree p").y_label("Point interpolations").y_limits(0,105);
  auto layout=dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2); layout.add(family).add(cost);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  layout.size(1100,490).fit_panels().save_svg("build/de_boor_theory.svg");
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame checks; checks.add_column("degree",degrees); checks.add_column("updates",updates);
  checks.add_column("exact_updates",exact_counts); checks.add_column("max_abs_y_error",errors);
  checks.add_column("tiny_endpoint_error",endpoint_errors);
  std::print("{}\n",checks.to_md(3));
}
```
