\image(figures/de_boor_theory.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Analytic curve values and actual update counts for twelve degrees. Very small absolute coordinate errors are printed with enough digits to distinguish rounding from exact equality.)
\alttext(Left: curves for degrees one, two, four and twelve approach the parabola as degree increases. Right: recorded interpolation counts lie on p times p plus one divided by two.)

The largest closed-form coordinate error is 3.331e-16, and the tiny-domain endpoint
error is exactly zero at all twelve degrees. Separate independent checks use R
`splineDesign` and SciPy `BSpline` on 29 curves and 3668 sample parameters, including
nonuniform, repeated, unclamped, tiny and translated knot sequences. Both agree
within 1.8e-15; 509 recorded interpolation steps also agree with exact rational
calculations on the stored binary inputs within 4.5e-16 in their coordinates.
These are numerical checks of the
evaluator, not error bounds for an arbitrary curve or knot sequence.

>> Local control: move one coefficient, change four cubic spans

Use ten cubic controls on knots \((0,0,0,0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,7,7,7)\), then move
only \(P_4\) upwards by two. Linearity gives a stronger prediction than a visual comparison:

$$
 \Delta C(t)=B_{4,3}(t)(0,2),\qquad
 \Delta C(t)=0\quad\text{outside }[u_4,u_8]=[1,5].
$$
\alttext(Moving control four upward by two moves the curve upward by twice its cubic basis weight. The change vanishes outside the four-span support from parameter one to five.)

For this simple-knot interior basis, the weight also vanishes at both support endpoints.
The right panel compares the observed displacement with an independent basis evaluation
through `fda::BSplineBasis`; it is not merely a second call to the same curve evaluator.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/de_boor_local_control.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const std::vector<double> knots{0,0,0,0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,7,7,7};
  std::vector<dm::geometry::Point2D> control{{0,0},{1,2},{2,-1},{3,3},{4,1},{5,4},{6,0},{7,2},{8,1},{9,0}};
  const dm::geometry::DeBoorSpline original(3,knots,control);
  control[4].y+=2; const dm::geometry::DeBoorSpline changed(3,knots,control);
  const auto t=dm::seql(0,7,281); const auto before=original.sample_table(t.values()), after=changed.sample_table(t.values());
  const dm::Vector<> displacement=dm::Vector<>(after.numeric_column("y").values())-dm::Vector<>(before.numeric_column("y").values());
  const auto B=dm::fda::BSplineBasis(3,knots).evaluate_dense(t.values());
  auto curves=original.plot_curve(), influence=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  curves.lines(after.numeric_column("x").values(),after.numeric_column("y").values(),"Moved P4",{220,90,35},3)
    .title("Moving one control has local influence").y_limits(-1.5,6.5);
  influence.lines(t.values(),(2*dm::Vector<>(B.col(4))).values(),"2 B4(t)",{80,80,80},3)
    .points(t.values(),displacement.values(),"Observed delta",{37,99,235},2)
    .abline_v(1,{150,150,150}).abline_v(5,{150,150,150})
    .title("Displacement equals its basis weight").x_label("Parameter t").y_label("Change in curve y").y_limits(-.1,1.9);
  auto layout=dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2); layout.add(curves).add(influence);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  layout.size(1100,490).fit_panels().save_svg("build/de_boor_local_control.svg");
  auto checks=original.sample_table({0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7});
  const auto moved=changed.sample_table({0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7});
  checks.add_column("delta_y",(dm::Vector<>(moved.numeric_column("y").values())-dm::Vector<>(checks.numeric_column("y").values())).values());
  std::print("{}\n",checks.select({"t","span","first_control","last_control","delta_y"}).to_md(6));
}
```
