\caption(Only the support of control four responds to its displacement. The zero-based active-control indices are candidate contributors on the selected span; a weight can vanish at a span boundary.)
\alttext(Left: the original cubic and the curve after moving control four upward differ only in the middle portion. Right: the observed vertical change overlays twice the independently evaluated cubic basis, is zero outside one to five, and peaks at four thirds near three.)

> A larger construction: the original clamped cubic

Return to the original six controls \((0,0),(1,4),(3,5),(5,1),(7,4),(8,0)\), with
knots \((0,0,0,0,1,2,3,3,3,3)\). Simple interior knots give a \(C^2\) curve.
At \(t=1.5\), span \(k=4\) uses controls one through four. Its first round has
weights \((3/4,1/2,1/4)\) in increasing local-index order, its second has
\((3/4,1/4)\), and its final weight is \(1/2\). The result is

$$
 C(1.5)=(4,49/16)=(4,3.0625),\qquad C(0)=(0,0),\qquad C(3)=(8,0).
$$
\alttext(The original cubic evaluates to four, 49 sixteenths at parameter one and a half, and exactly to its first and last controls at parameters zero and three.)

The curve generally passes near interior controls rather than through them. The table
also shows why uniformly spaced parameter values need not produce uniformly spaced
points in the plane. Dense sampling approximates the shape; it does not certify a
geometric error tolerance or yield an arc-length parameterisation.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/de_boor_cubic.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const dm::geometry::DeBoorSpline spline(3,{0,0,0,0,1,2,3,3,3,3},{{0,0},{1,4},{3,5},{5,1},{7,4},{8,0}});
  const auto trace=spline.trace(1.5);
  auto curve=spline.plot_curve(), construction=trace.plot();
  curve.points({trace.point.x},{trace.point.y},"t = 1.5",{220,90,35},6)
    .title("Clamped cubic: exact endpoint controls").y_limits(-.5,8);
  construction.title("Six interpolations from four controls").y_limits(-.5,8);
  auto layout=dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2); layout.add(curve).add(construction);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  layout.size(1100,490).fit_panels().save_svg("build/de_boor_cubic.svg");
  std::print("{}\n\n{}\n",spline.sample_table({0,.5,1,1.5,2,2.5,3}).to_md(6),
             trace.table().select({"round","local","alpha","x","y"}).to_md(6));
}
```
